# MCP

- Implement tools in `clients/public_api.py`, then wire thin `@mcp.tool()` wrappers in client adapters.
- Keep tool names identical across Claude, ChatGPT, and Gemini adapters (`PUBLIC_TOOL_NAMES` — currently 16 tools).
- Validate/sanitize untrusted inputs with `core.security.input.sanitize_payload`.
- Remote HTTP transports require `MCP_AUTH_TOKEN` or `MCP_API_KEY`; never ship wildcard CORS in production remote mode.
- After tool changes: run `./scripts/check.sh` (tool discovery) and MCP smoke tests.
- Local start: `./scripts/run-mcp.sh` (stdio) or `./scripts/run-mcp.sh http`.
